.\" SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Ingo Ruhnke <grumbel@gmail.com>
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
.TH GLOBTOO 1 "2026-11" "Globtoo @PROJECT_VERSION_FULL@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
globtoo \- interactive 3D Earth globe and projected world maps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B globtoo
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ earth-texture.jpg ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B globtoo
is a tactile Earth viewer with a freely rotatable 3D globe, smooth zoom,
animated transitions to four flat projections, country borders and names,
and an optional geographic grid and distance scale.
The starting view is oriented to the system timezone unless overridden with
.BR \-\-center .
.PP
The on-screen toolbar controls projection, shading, texture, political
colors, borders, labels, capitals, cities, rivers, and grid. It also includes a compass and reset control.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show full command-line help and exit without initializing graphics.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the full version (including Git metadata on development builds) and exit.
.TP
.BI \-m\  "COORDS" ", " \-\-marker\  "COORDS"
Add a geographic marker. Append
.BI "|" label
inside the coordinate argument to label it. Repeat as needed.
.TP
.BI \-\-marker-lonlat\  "COORDS"
Add a marker using longitude,latitude order (common in GIS formats).
.TP
.BI \-l\  "TEXT" ", " \-\-label\  "TEXT"
Set the label of the most recently added marker.
.TP
.BI \-\-marker-file\  "FILE"
Read a file containing latitude,longitude[,label] CSV records or
coordinate | label records. Blank lines and comments are ignored.
.TP
.BI \-\-marker-color\  "#RRGGBB"
Set the color of subsequently added markers (default: #FFC54B).
.TP
.BI \-\-marker-size\  "PIXELS"
Set the radius in pixels (2 through 32) of subsequently added markers.
.TP
.BI \-\-center\  "COORDS"
Center the startup view on the given latitude,longitude.
.TP
.BI \-\-texture\  "FILE"
Load the supplied equirectangular Earth image instead of the built-in one.
A positional file name may be used for compatibility.
.TP
.BI \--layer\  "imagery|relief|elevation|population"
Choose the starting raster layer. Relief requires an installed visual tile set;
elevation requires signed, measured-height tiles; population requires measured
people-per-square-kilometre tiles with a year and physical-unit legend.
.TP
.BI \--imagery-dir\  "DIR"
Use a prepared high-resolution Earth imagery tile set in the ordinary
Imagery mode. Close views load geographic JPEG tiles lazily; distant views
and projection transitions retain the ordinary Earth base texture. The
folder must contain a valid
.B manifest.txt
and the generated tiles.
.TP
.BI \--body\  "NAME"
Select the body whose globe or projected map is displayed, for example
.BR earth ", " mars ", " titan " or " pluto .
Press M (Shift+M backwards) or use the NEXT > / < PREV buttons to cycle
bodies. Earth-only country, city, river and thematic
layers are suppressed on other bodies.
.TP
.BI \--focus\  "NAME"
Select a built-in named planetary feature (case-insensitive), switch to its
body and start centered on its Gazetteer location. Conflicting explicit
\--body or \--center options are rejected. Example:
.B globtoo --focus 'Olympus Mons'
.TP
.B \--list-bodies
Print every selectable body with its name, kind (planet, dwarf planet or
moon), parent body and mean radius, without starting SDL. Gas giants are
shown at their cloud tops.
.TP
.B \--list-features
Print the available IAU Gazetteer planetary landmark names and their
approximate east-positive coordinates, without starting SDL.
.TP
.BI \--body-texture\  "BODY=FILE"
Use a normalized small equirectangular texture for the selected body;
repeatable. See the planetary maps documentation for source longitude
conventions.
.TP
.BI \--body-imagery-dir\  "BODY=DIR"
Provide high-resolution tiles for any body. Repeatable;
the manifest, 2048-pixel preview and power-of-two tiles are loaded from the
specified directory. The source must be normalized to east-positive,
north-up, 180 degrees west at the left edge. The build-time tile converter
can perform longitude-direction and 0/180-degree seam normalization.
.TP
.BI \--relief-dir\  "DIR"
Use a locally prepared high-resolution raster tile set, with
.B manifest.txt
and JPEG tiles. See the installed raster-layer documentation.
.TP
.BI \--elevation-dir\  "DIR"
Use measured land elevation and ocean bathymetry tiles with
.B legend.txt
and
.BR manifest.txt .
Signed elevation and depth values are expressed in metres, with the source
and reference year displayed by the ELEV control.
.TP
.BI \--population-dir\  "DIR"
Use locally prepared numeric population density (people per square kilometre)
tiles and a logarithmic-scale legend recording source, resolution, and year.
The data is optional and is not fetched on application launch.
.TP
.BI \-\-download-asset\  "earth"
Explicitly fetch the pinned Earth base map to the user's XDG cache and exit
without starting SDL. Requires a build compiled with the libcurl downloader
(enabled in the Nix
.B globtoo-lite
package). The full offline Nix package does not include the downloader.
No network access occurs during normal launches. A corrupt or interrupted
transfer never replaces an existing cached file.
See the installed DOWNLOADS documentation for the URL and digest.
.SH COORDINATES
By default, coordinate pairs are latitude first, longitude second, in degrees.
North and east are positive. Accepted forms include:
.TP
.B "52.5200,13.4050"
Decimal degrees (Berlin).
.TP
.B "51.5074 N, 0.1278 W"
Hemisphere letters, prefixed or suffixed.
.TP
.B "51:30:26N, 0:07:39W"
Degrees, minutes, seconds; symbols are accepted too.
.TP
.B "51\(de30.5'N, 0\(de7.25'W"
Degrees and decimal minutes.
.TP
.B "geo:52.52,13.405"
RFC 5870 Geo URI (altitude is accepted but not displayed).
.TP
.B "+52.52+013.405/"
ISO 6709 signed coordinate pair.
.SH MOUSE CONTROLS
.TP
.B Left-drag
Rotate the globe, or rotate and reproject Earth in a flat map.
.TP
.B Middle-drag
Pan the 2D map like a paper sheet; on the 3D globe, roll the view.
.TP
.B Shift + left-drag or Shift + middle-drag
Roll the map around the view center (unless North Lock is enabled).
.TP
.B Mouse wheel
Zoom in or out with small, reciprocal increments.
.TP
.B Two-finger pinch
Spread two fingers to zoom in or bring them together to zoom out in any projection.
.TP
.B Two-finger twist
Twist two fingers on a touchscreen to roll the globe or flat map when North Lock is off.
.SH KEYBOARD CONTROLS
.TP
.B F
Toggle the approximate named planetary landmark overlay on solid-surface bodies,
including when the screen controls are hidden.
.TP
.B M, Shift + M
Switch to the next or previous body in the catalog.
.TP
.B Tab
Hide or restore the on-screen toolbar, compass and distance scale.
Country names, markers and the optional geographic grid remain visible.
.TP
.B G
Toggle Grab / Arcball control mode for the 3D globe. The same toggle
is available below Reset in the compass panel. North Lock, also in the
compass panel, keeps the geographic north direction pointing up during drags.
.TP
.B 1, 2, 3, 4, 5
Choose globe, Plate Carree, Mercator, Mollweide, or Hammer projection.
.TP
.B Space, B, N, P, V
Toggle shading, borders, country names, political colors, or Earth texture.
.TP
.B T
Toggle trackball relative-mouse mode when viewing the 3D globe.
.TP
.B Escape
Exit trackball mode, or quit Globtoo.
.SH GAMEPAD CONTROLS
Globtoo uses the first available SDL-mapped controller while the window has focus.
.TP
.B Left stick
Rotate the globe or move the flat map.
.TP
.B Left / right trigger
Zoom out / in continuously.
.TP
.B Left / right shoulder
Zoom out / in one step.
.TP
.B D-pad
Move the pointer.
.TP
.B South face button (A / Cross)
Click an on-screen control, or hold while moving the pointer to drag.
.TP
.B Start
Hide or restore the on-screen controls. On R36S, quit Globtoo.
.SH VIEWS
The GUI provides a globe and four projections: equirectangular (Plate
Carr\('ee), Mercator, Mollweide, and Hammer. The map transforms smoothly
between the views. Layers can be independently enabled, including blending
Earth texture beneath translucent political colors. Capitals are shown as
geographically anchored diamonds and major cities as dots; ranked rivers and
more cities are revealed at closer zoom. A Relief button selects the optional
high-resolution topography and ocean-bathymetry imagery when installed. The
ELEV button selects measured elevation and bathymetry, with a metres legend
and source attribution, when separately installed. POP selects optional
population density maps with a people/km2 legend and reference year.
Their visibility toggles are in the
bottom toolbar. Supplied Natural Earth data is preprocessed into compact
binary assets during build, with no runtime downloads.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GLOBE_ASSET_DIR
Optional override for the resource directory, which should contain
.B assets/
and
.B shaders/
subdirectories, and optionally \fBimagery/\fR (with \fBimagery/moon/\fR etc.),
\fBrelief/\fR, \fBelevation/\fR and \fBpopulation/\fR directories. Otherwise,
Globtoo searches next to a development binary
or in its installation data directory. The executable can be launched from
any working directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_DATADIR@/globtoo/
Installed Earth imagery, compiled country meshes, ranked geographic overlays, and shaders.
.TP
.I @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_DATADIR@/applications/io.github.Grumbel.globtoo.desktop
Desktop launcher.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.B globtoo --marker '52.52,13.405|Berlin'
.B globtoo --marker 'geo:48.8583,2.2945' --label 'Eiffel Tower'
.B globtoo --marker-file places.csv --center '48.8583,2.2945'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The Globtoo README and the included docs/MARKERS.md document further
formats and navigation details.
